// Devon village longhouse — typical c.1300 rural dwelling.
// Sources: Beresford & Hurst, "Wharram: a Study of Settlement on
// the Yorkshire Wolds" (1990) — comparable Devon longhouse plans
// in Beresford, "The Lost Villages of England" (1954); NHLE
// listings for surviving Dartmoor longhouses (e.g. Higher
// Uppacott). 5×5 single-room footprint represents the human end
// of a longhouse; the byre end is omitted at this scale. Timber-
// framed with cob infill, modelled as WoodWall.
// The 2.5D facade reads as a front-on house: a tiled roof up top, a
// timber wall band below, windows set into the walls and a door at
// front-centre. The door faces south (the `.` gap in the bottom wall)
// so the player walks up into it; stepping onto any interior cell
// suppresses this building's roof and the single room shows through
// (roof-reveal, see flora::Roof). Roof char -> Sheet::Structures (col, row):
//   l/m/r  roof overhang (top edge)   L/M/R  roof body (full tiles)
//   W      timber wall   O  window    D  door
Prefab(
    tag: "house",
    tier: Village,
    variant: "cottage",
    weight: 5,
    size: (5, 5),
    palette: {
        '#': WoodWall,
        '.': Floor,
    },
    grid: [
        "#####",
        "#...#",
        "#...#",
        "#...#",
        "##.##",
    ],
    roof_palette: {
        'l': (5, 1), 'm': (6, 1), 'r': (7, 1),
        'L': (5, 2), 'M': (6, 2), 'R': (7, 2),
        'W': (8, 30),
        'O': (4, 38),
        'D': (0, 42),
    },
    roof: [
        "lmmmr",
        "LMMMR",
        "WOWOW",
        "WWWWW",
        "WWDWW",
    ],
)
